# Line endings for the Gradle wrapper.
#
# `gradlew` is a POSIX shell script: it must keep LF endings in the working copy even
# when cloned on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, or it fails under git-bash/WSL with
# `\r: command not found`. `gradlew.bat` is the opposite — a Windows batch file that
# wants CRLF. The wrapper jar is binary and must never be line-ending translated.
gradlew         text eol=lf
gradlew.bat     text eol=crlf
*.jar           binary
